CORRECTED, 2026-08-19 (ticket 004, M1). This file previously recorded the
old MicroPython exploration's yield fix verbatim
(reference/FINDINGS.md Section 3b): adding `schedule()` inside
`microbit_hal_background_processing()`. That function is also called from
this port's STOCK (unpatched) `MICROPY_VM_HOOK_POLL` in mpconfigport.h --
confirmed by diffing a fresh checkout against its own git HEAD, the
MICROPY_VM_HOOK_COUNT/INIT/POLL/LOOP/RETURN block is upstream default
behavior, not one of this project's own patches. Applying the old diff
therefore put a fiber-switching `schedule()` call on a path reachable
from INSIDE VM bytecode dispatch -- the exact heap-corruption landmine
docs/nezha-upy-review.md Section 1 / docs/design/specification.md
Section 7.1 describe, and the most likely mechanism behind the observed
gopiv 2026-08-14 HardFault this ledger already attributes to
"fiber switches from VM/GC hooks."

The diff below is the CORRECTED version: it touches ONLY
microbit_hal_idle(), never microbit_hal_background_processing(). See
patches/apply_yield.py's own module docstring for the full reasoning --
that script is what actually applies this (idempotent Python text
replace, not `git apply`, matching every other build.sh patch step's
convention); this file is kept as the documented, reviewable diff, not as
something `patch`/`git apply` is run against directly.

--- a/src/codal_app/microbithal.cpp
+++ b/src/codal_app/microbithal.cpp
@@ -89,7 +89,14 @@ void microbit_hal_background_processing(void) {
 }

 void microbit_hal_idle(void) {
-    microbit_hal_background_processing();
-    __WFI();
+    // Cooperative yield to the kernel fiber (native/platform_ports.h's
+    // FiberLauncher/Sleeper) -- the ONLY yield point in this image; see
+    // this file's own module docstring for why it is scoped to exactly
+    // this function and not to microbit_hal_background_processing()
+    // (which the stock MICROPY_VM_HOOK_POLL also calls, and which must
+    // therefore stay fiber-switch-free).
+    codal::fiber_sleep(1);
+    microbit_hal_background_processing();
 }

Deliberately NOT part of this patch, permanently: a MICROPY_GC_HOOK_LOOP
addition to mpconfigport.h. Nothing in this design needs the kernel fiber
woken from inside a GC sweep -- only from main-context idle() -- so no
corrected version of that half exists to apply.
